1. Idempotency Check via CIB.API.FT

Current behavior (T24):
Every inbound request carries a unique MSG.ID. Before processing, the service checks a shared audit table (CIB.API.FT) for a prior record with that same MSG.ID. If a matching record already exists with a status of successful completion, the service does NOT reprocess the request — it simply returns the previously stored result (the same FT ID, OFS record, and paid amount from the original successful call). This protects us against duplicate transaction creation when a channel retries a request (e.g. after a timeout) without knowing whether the original attempt actually succeeded.

This same table and mechanism is shared across several of our services (Create Outward Transfer, Create Nostro Transfer, and the Authorise step, among others), so it functions as a common idempotency layer across the whole funds transfer family rather than being service-specific.

